Villages, golden houses, honey, honey, they are awake. May all the gods be pleased with the Brahmins. 3. Meaning of the word:
Gavah—cow; Hiranyam—gold; Vasansi—cloth; Madhu—sweet; Madhu—mixed with honey; Annam—food; Aadrutah—with respect;
Brahmanebhyah—to the Brahmins; Daduh—given; Sarve—all; Devah—Lord; Nah—to us; Priyatam—please be pleased; Iti—Thus;
While praying. The Gwals gave cows, gold, clothes and a mixture of spices as offerings to the Brahmins. Then they prayed, “Our Lord, be pleased with us that we may be honored with You.””

Drink water from the banks of the Saraswati, those who have taken a vow. The great fortunes of the night, the Nandas and the Sanandas. 4>. Meaning of the word:
Oosu- stayed; Saraswati- shore—shore of Saraswati; Jalam— water; Praashya- after eating (drinking); Yat- Vratah- difficult vow;
While doing; Rajanim- at night; Tam- that; Maha- fortunate; Nand- Sunandak- origin; Nand- Nand, Sunand etc.
Nanda, Sunanda, and other extremely fortunate cowherds spent that night on the banks of Saraswati, with restraint,
keeping their respective vows. He only drank the water and fasted. Meaning: Srila Viswanatha Chakravarthy Thakur says that Sunandan Nanda was the younger brother of Maharaj. Someone who is very hungry in the midst of a great famine. Yadrichayaagato nandam shayanam urgo aagraasit. 5. Meaning of the word:
Someone—anyone; Great—big; Serpent—by the snake; In that—in that; In the forest—in the area of the forest; Very hungry—extremely hungry;
By chance—by chance; Arrived—arrived; Nandam—to Nand Maharaj; Sleeping—sleeping; Ura-gah—swallowing with the stomach;
Agrasit—swallowed. At night, a huge and extremely hungry snake appeared in that forest. That sleeping Nand
Went near the Maharaj, crawling on his stomach, and started swallowing them. Sah Chukroshiha, Krishna Krishna Mahanayam. The snake devours, the father is pleased, but he is released. 6. Lexicon
